// LIVE version of sentinel-rules/queries/waf-repeated-blocks.kql (Aayush, Person 2).
// Analytics rule "ATDR – Repeated WAF blocks from one client": High, every 5 min, lookback 15 min.
// Changes from the original (checked against atdr-law, 2026-10-23):
//  - Window and threshold unchanged: >= 5 distinct blocked transactions from one ClientIp in 15 min.
//    Real data: one T1-T6 run produced 6 (2 managed-rule blocks + 4 RateLimitDemo blocks).
//  - Action =~ "Blocked" kept: on DRS 2.1 the individual rules log "Matched"; the block decision is
//    one row per transaction (RuleId 949110 for managed rules, RateLimitDemo for the rate limit).
//  - Added VmResourceId (the protected backend VM) for the AzureResource entity mapping.
//    __PROTECTED_VM_ID__ is replaced by detection-live/deploy-rules.sh at deploy time.
AGWFirewallLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(15m)
| where Action =~ "Blocked"
| where isnotempty(ClientIp) and isnotempty(TransactionId)
| summarize
    blockedEvents = count(),
    blockedTransactions = dcount(TransactionId),
    ruleIds = make_set(RuleId, 20),
    sampleUris = make_set(RequestUri, 5),
    firstSeen = min(TimeGenerated),
    lastSeen = max(TimeGenerated)
    by ClientIp
| where blockedTransactions >= 5
| project
    TimeGenerated = lastSeen,
    ClientIp,
    blockedEvents,
    blockedTransactions,
    ruleIds,
    sampleUris,
    firstSeen,
    lastSeen
| extend VmResourceId = "__PROTECTED_VM_ID__"
